In short (the licence text is what binds): you may copy, share and modify the
project, publicly too, provided that:
  - you credit the author and link to the project, and say what you changed
    in a modified version;
  - you do not use it for commercial purposes;
  - you share a modified version under the same licence.

How to credit:
  Metin2 Playerbots - Tieru - https://github.com/TieruYT/metin2-playerbots - CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

The licence covers the work of the project's authors: code, scripts, data,
graphics and documentation. It does not cover Metin2 (Ymir Interactive,
Webzen), the server-file packages, third-party libraries or parts that carry a
licence of their own. Versions up to and including 2.2.16 were released under
the MIT licence (LICENSE-MIT.txt) and stay under it. Details and the author's
additional permissions (voluntary donations towards a server, recording
gameplay) are in NOTICE.md.
